  <data name="HelpTrouble2.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>GoXLR not controllable: quit the official GoXLR App (tray icon → Exit). Only one program can control the device.</value></data>
  <data name="HelpTrouble3.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>No meter on Line In / Console: these analog inputs report no level over USB.</value></data>
  <data name="HelpControlsTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Controls</value></data>
  <data name="HelpControls1.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Faders: drag the cap (Shift = fine), scroll the mouse wheel (Ctrl = fine), or use the arrow keys.</value></data>
  <data name="HelpControls2.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Knobs: drag up/down, scroll, or use the arrow keys. Double-click resets to the default.</value></data>
  <data name="HelpControls3.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Mute: the fader drops to 0 and returns to its previous position when you unmute.</value></data>
  <data name="HelpControlsMixerPages.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Mixer Pages (GoXLR Fader Banks): Switch between Page 1 and Page 2 in the Mixer view. On GoXLR hardware, pressing the active Sampler Bank A button again (or pressing MUTE + !@#$?* together) toggles motorized faders to the second bank.</value></data>
